<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="A question of possible futures. Explore public research, publications and events." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#10111f" />
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://boomerrawlings.com/ACF/" />
    <title>A question of futures</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/ACF/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/ACF/style.css?v=regions-20261012" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/ACF/entry-effects.css?v=regions-20261012" />
    <script is:inline src="/ACF/entry.js?v=regions-20261012" defer></script>
    <script is:inline type="module" src="/ACF/app.js?v=regions-20261012"></script>
  </head>
  <body class="entry-pending" data-view="map">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#search">Skip to collection search</a>

    <section id="entry-screen" aria-labelledby="entry-heading">
      <div class="entry-prompt" id="entry-prompt">
        <h1 id="entry-heading" class="sr-only">Opening riddle</h1>
        <blockquote class="riddle">
          I hold worlds that do not yet exist,<br />
          and chart the paths where futures split.<br />
          I bear their weight, yet have no hands.<br />
          <em>What am I?</em>
        </blockquote>
        <form id="entry-form" novalidate>
          <label for="entry-input">Your answer</label>
          <div class="answer-field">
            <input id="entry-input" name="answer" type="text" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="characters" spellcheck="false" maxlength="80" enterkeyhint="go" aria-describedby="entry-feedback" placeholder="Five letters…" />
            <button id="entry-submit" type="submit" aria-label="Enter the collection">Enter <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
          </div>
          <p id="entry-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </form>
        <a class="entry-backlink" href="/">Back to Boomer Rawlings</a>
      </div>
      <div id="entry-sequence" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
        <div class="entry-word">
          <span class="entry-letter" id="atlas-letter-0">A</span><span class="entry-letter" id="atlas-letter-1">T</span><span class="entry-letter" id="atlas-letter-2">L</span><span class="entry-letter" id="atlas-letter-3">A</span><span class="entry-letter" id="atlas-letter-4">S</span>
          <svg id="entry-constellation" viewBox="0 0 400 250" aria-hidden="true">
            <g id="entry-links"><path d="M30 140 125 50 195 155 280 90 370 175M30 140 195 155 370 175M125 50 280 90" /></g>
            <circle id="entry-star-0" cx="30" cy="140" r="2.5" /><circle id="entry-star-1" cx="125" cy="50" r="2.5" /><circle id="entry-star-2" cx="195" cy="155" r="2.5" /><circle id="entry-star-3" cx="280" cy="90" r="2.5" /><circle id="entry-star-4" cx="370" cy="175" r="2.5" />
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p id="entry-loading" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>Preparing the full collection…</p>
      <button id="skip-animation" class="text-button" type="button" hidden>Skip animation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
      <noscript><p class="noscript-note">This interactive collection needs JavaScript. The <a href="https://ieet.org/publications/">IEET publication directory</a> is available without it.</p></noscript>
    </section>

    <div id="atlas-workspace" hidden inert>
      <header class="atlas-header">
        <button id="return-entry" class="atlas-brand" type="button" aria-label="Return to the opening riddle"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">A<span class="brand-star">✳</span></span><span>The Atlas <small>of Contested Futures</small></span></button>
        <div class="header-right"><p id="dataset-status" class="dataset-status"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Preparing the collection</p><button id="about-open" class="quiet-button" type="button">About <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div>
      </header>

      <div class="explore-toolbar" role="search" aria-label="Explore the collection">
        <label class="search-field" for="search"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="m16 16 5 5"/></svg><span class="sr-only">Search titles, authors and topics</span><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Find an idea, a person, a possible future…" autocomplete="off" /></label>
        <div class="toolbar-filters">
          <label class="filter-field" for="type-filter"><span>Show</span><select id="type-filter"><option value="">All types</option></select></label>
          <fieldset class="year-filter"><legend class="sr-only">Record years</legend><label for="year-from" class="sr-only">From year</label><input id="year-from" type="number" min="1000" max="2200" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="From" /><span aria-hidden="true">—</span><label for="year-to" class="sr-only">To year</label><input id="year-to" type="number" min="1000" max="2200" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="To" /></fieldset>
          <button id="collections-open" class="collection-button" type="button"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m10 2 8 4-8 4-8-4 8-4Zm-8 8 8 4 8-4M2 14l8 4 8-4"/></svg>Collections</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <main id="main" class="atlas-main" tabindex="-1">
        <section id="catalog-scale" class="catalog-scale" aria-label="Full collection by record type">
          <div class="scale-copy"><p id="scale-total">The full collection</p><p id="scale-legend">Every loaded record, across all types</p></div>
          <svg id="scale-bar" viewBox="0 0 1000 8" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="Record type distribution across every loaded record" width="100%" height="8"></svg>
        </section>
        <div class="exploration-bar"><nav id="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Current exploration"><span>All connections</span></nav><div class="view-switch" role="group" aria-label="Display"><button id="map-view" type="button" aria-pressed="true">Map</button><button id="list-view" type="button" aria-pressed="false">List</button></div></div>
        <details id="map-layers" class="map-layers">
          <summary>Map layers <span>Every record has a point</span></summary>
          <div class="layer-options" role="group" aria-label="Map layers">
            <label><input id="labels-toggle" type="checkbox" checked />Labels</label>
            <label><input id="names-toggle" type="checkbox" />Catalog-local names</label>
            <label><input id="relationships-toggle" type="checkbox" />Source routes</label>
            <label><input id="themes-toggle" type="checkbox" />Inferred routes</label>
            <label><input id="regions-toggle" type="checkbox" checked />Theme regions</label>
          </div>
          <p class="layer-explanation">Labels are limited for readability. Point and route data are not sampled; overlapping points remain separate records. Solid routes show source credits or recorded relationships; dashed routes show inferred matches. Routes do not establish citation, influence or agreement.</p>
          <div id="region-evidence"><p>Regions and proximity are illustrative, not an objective taxonomy. Membership comes only from English title keywords. Boundaries do not contain every member: overlapping memberships share positions. Select a group to inspect literal matches, unknown dates, source credits and documented relationships. No affiliation, agreement, citation or influence is implied. Collections remain a provenance lens.</p></div>
        </details>
        <section class="region-navigation" aria-label="Title-word regions">
          <div class="region-navigation-heading"><span>Title-word regions · illustrative</span><p id="region-union">Unique record memberships; overlapping groups.</p></div>
          <div id="region-memberships" role="group" aria-label="Explore a region"></div>
        </section>
        <div class="atlas-panels">
          <section id="graph-stage" class="graph-stage" aria-labelledby="graph-heading">
            <div class="graph-intro"><h1 id="graph-heading">A field of possible futures</h1><p id="graph-subtitle">Every record has a point. Follow one back to its source.</p></div>
            <canvas id="network" tabindex="0" aria-label="Interactive publication network. Hover or tap a node for metadata." aria-describedby="graph-instructions graph-keyboard-instructions"></canvas>
            <p id="graph-instructions" class="graph-instructions">Hover or tap for metadata · Drag to pan · Scroll or pinch to zoom</p>
            <p id="graph-keyboard-instructions" class="sr-only">Focus the map and use arrow keys to preview nodes, Enter to pin a preview, Shift plus arrow keys to pan, and Escape to dismiss. Previous node and Next node also browse previews. Use the collection list to access every record.</p>
            <aside id="node-preview" class="node-preview" aria-label="Node preview" hidden>
              <div class="preview-header"><p id="preview-kind" class="preview-kind"></p><button id="preview-close" class="preview-close" type="button" aria-label="Close node preview">×</button></div>
              <h2 id="preview-title"></h2>
              <p id="preview-collection" class="preview-collection"></p>
              <p id="preview-meta" class="preview-meta"></p>
              <p id="preview-context" class="preview-context"></p>
              <button id="preview-open" class="preview-open" type="button">Open record <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>
            </aside>
            <p id="preview-announcement" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <div class="graph-controls"><button id="zoom-in" type="button" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button><button id="zoom-out" type="button" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button><button id="reset-view" type="button" aria-label="Reset map view"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7a7 7 0 1 1-1 6M4 2v5h5"/></svg></button><span class="control-divider" aria-hidden="true"></span><button id="motion-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Toggle map motion"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 4v12M15 4v12"/></svg></button></div>
            <div id="preview-navigation" class="preview-navigation" role="group" aria-label="Browse node previews"><button id="preview-prev" type="button" aria-label="Previous node"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span><span class="preview-nav-label">Previous node</span></button><button id="preview-next" type="button" aria-label="Next node"><span class="preview-nav-label">Next node</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></div>
            <div class="graph-bottom"><p id="graph-status" aria-live="off">Loading public metadata…</p><div class="graph-legend" aria-label="Relationship legend"><span><i class="documented-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>Source-documented</span><span><i class="inferred-line" aria-hidden="true"></i>Inferred</span></div></div>
          </section>

          <aside class="records-panel" aria-labelledby="results-heading">
            <header class="records-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">The reading room</p><h2 id="results-heading">Explore the collection</h2></div><span id="results-count" class="count-pill">…</span></header>
            <div id="results" class="results"></div>
            <div class="load-more-wrap"><button id="load-more" class="load-more" type="button">More from the collection <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></button></div>
            <p class="records-footnote">Metadata, people, and paths back to the source.</p>
          </aside>

          <aside id="region-panel" class="detail-panel region-panel" aria-label="Selected region" hidden><button id="region-close" class="detail-close" type="button" aria-label="Close region details">Close <span aria-hidden="true">×</span></button><div id="region-content"></div></aside>
          <aside id="detail" class="detail-panel" aria-label="Selected record" hidden><button id="detail-close" class="detail-close" type="button" aria-label="Close selected record">Close <span aria-hidden="true">×</span></button><div id="detail-content"></div></aside>
        </div>
      </main>
      <footer class="atlas-footer"><span>A living map, an incomplete territory.</span><a href="/">Boomer Rawlings <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></footer>
    </div>

    <dialog id="collections-dialog" aria-labelledby="collections-heading"><div class="dialog-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Shape your atlas</p><h2 id="collections-heading">Collections</h2></div><form method="dialog"><button class="dialog-close" aria-label="Close collections">×</button></form></div><p class="dialog-intro">All nine public catalogs open together. Choose which collections to display, or add compatible metadata. Names remain separate within each catalog.</p><div id="collection-options"></div><div class="import-box"><label for="import-file">Bring another collection</label><p>Import a metadata catalog in JSON or JSONL format. Imports stay in this browser session; no upload.</p><input id="import-file" type="file" disabled accept=".json,.jsonl,application/json,application/x-ndjson" /><p id="import-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><a href="/ACF/import-format.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View import format <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></dialog>

    <dialog id="about-dialog" aria-labelledby="about-heading"><div class="dialog-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Read the map</p><h2 id="about-heading">Many futures.<br />A shared atlas.</h2></div><form method="dialog"><button class="dialog-close" aria-label="Close about">×</button></form></div><p class="dialog-intro">The Atlas of Contested Futures connects public research, people and events around the futures we imagine, debate and build.</p><div class="about-grid"><section><h3>Begin anywhere</h3><p>Select a collection, search for an idea, or follow a node. Every loaded record is submitted as its own point. Zoom changes the view, not a sample. Names are an optional, separate layer of catalog-local labels. Positions and overlapping theme regions are illustrative. Labels are limited for readability; point and route data are not sampled. The reading room searches every record.</p></section><section><h3>Read connections carefully</h3><p>Solid lines represent relationships documented in source metadata. Dashed lines represent inferred thematic similarities, which you can turn on separately. Brief highlights emphasize existing connections without showing direction or causality. Themes come from overlapping English title-keyword matches; unmatched records remain searchable. A connection never implies agreement or endorsement.</p></section><section><h3>A map with open edges</h3><p>The initial collection draws on public IEET and separately collected related catalogs. Historical coverage is incomplete. Some dates and bylines are missing; possible duplicates and name ambiguities remain. Each record keeps its source evidence.</p></section><section><h3>Public by design</h3><p>The opening riddle is playful, not authentication. This site contains public metadata and links, not private research notes or full copyrighted articles. Additional catalogs are imported locally in your browser.</p></section></div><a class="source-link" href="/ACF/coverage.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Collection coverage and provenance <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></dialog>
  </body>
</html>
